<%#
  One project on the list. `thumb` is a Maker::Preview or nil (cover). The `.file-cell` +
  data-node-id wiring lets the shared `thumbs` controller poll a pending cover to ready — but only
  when a cover node exists. No cover -> a neutral placeholder, never a forever-spinner: the rail's
  projects icon (structural redesign slice 6; no emoji in the interface).
%>
<div class="project-tile">
  <%= link_to project_path(project), class: "project-card" do %>
    <% if project.cover_node_id %>
      <span class="thumb file-cell" data-thumbs-target="cell"
            data-node-id="<%= project.cover_node_id %>" data-ext="">
        <%= render "files/thumb", thumb:, ext_label: "", url: preview_src(thumb) %>
      </span>
    <% else %>
      <span class="thumb project-thumb-empty" aria-hidden="true"><%= rail_icon(:projects) %></span>
    <% end %>
    <span class="project-name"><%= project.name %></span>
  <% end %>
  <%#
    ONE STATUS BADGE PER CARD, ALWAYS (2026-11-02, the UX audit's C7). Every card on the seeded
    audit read "New" beside its status, and a planning project read nothing at all — two words for
    one state on some cards and none on others. Now every card carries exactly one, in the words
    and component classes the project page's own head uses, OUTSIDE the link (`.project-card
    .badge` stays empty, projects_flow_test.rb).

    "NEW" IS THE STATUS WORD OF A PROJECT THAT IS STILL NEW (stage 4, S4-6; story 1.1): an
    auto-created project the owner has not opened yet, still at the column's first status. That is
    the only feedback discovery has ever had, and the one that works on every backend and for the
    unattended 15-minute pass, which is how discovery actually runs. It takes the place of
    "Planning" rather than sitting beside it, and never beside a later status: a discovered project
    set to Done from its edit page is Done, not new. `discovered_at.present?` IS the definition of
    auto-created — Maker::ProjectDiscovery is the only writer, and Projects::AdoptionsController
    leaves it nil on purpose (a project you made is never new to you). It clears itself on the
    first open — ProjectsController#show stamps `opened_at` — so nothing has to be dismissed. All
    three columns come off the row this card already holds, so the badge costs no query on the
    index or on Recent.
  %>
  <% if project.status == "planning" && project.discovered_at.present? && project.opened_at.nil? %>
    <span class="badge project-new status-planning">New</span>
  <% else %>
    <span class="badge status-<%= project.status %>"><%= project.status.humanize %></span>
  <% end %>
  <%# THE KIND, WHERE THE PROJECT IS LISTED (stage 4, S4-7). A NON-DEFAULT kind only: `other` is
      the column default, and badging a default kind is noise (a status is different: it is always
      one of five things worth saying). Beside the status rather than inside the link_to, so the
      tile's badges are one group and none of them is part of the card's own click target.
      `.badge` is a component (design-system rule 3); `project-kind` is a qualifier, and
      components.css is not touched. The label comes from Maker::ProjectKind, never `kind.humanize`
      -- "Cnc" is not a word. %>
  <% unless project.kind == Maker::ProjectKind::DEFAULT %>
    <span class="badge project-kind"><%= Maker::ProjectKind.label(project.kind) %></span>
  <% end %>
  <% if project.status == "archived" %>
    <%= button_to "Unarchive", unarchive_project_path(project), method: :patch, class: "linkbtn" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
